  ('404628628928613806', 'Clerks', 2000, 'Animation, Comedy', 'Kevin Smith, David Mandel, Scott Mosier', null, 'Brian O''Halloran, Jeff Anderson, Jason Mewes, Kevin Smith, Alec Baldwin, Kevin Michael Richardson, Charles Barkley, Dan Etheridge', 'TV-14', 'The continuing adventures of store clerks Dante and Randal, who try to make the best of their menial labor, with no help from Jay and Silent Bob.', 'The continuing adventures of store clerks Dante and Randal, who try to make the best of their menial labor, with no help from Jay and Silent Bob.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xunXvzFlkf1GGgMkCySA9CCFumB.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:2'),
  ('697095762601571723', 'Clevatess', 2025, 'Animation, Action & Adventure, Sci-Fi & Fantasy', null, null, 'Haruka Shiraishi, Mutsumi Tamura, Yuichi Nakamura, Saya Aizawa, Aoi Yuuki, Hiroki Yasumoto, Chiharu Shigematsu, Tomoyo Kurosawa', null, 'One of the Lords of Dark Beasts, Clevatess’s reign shatters when he revives a hero he personally slayed and adopts an orphaned humanoid baby—the last hope to save a dying world. Now bound together, what fate awaits this unlikely trio?', 'One of the Lords of Dark Beasts, Clevatess’s reign shatters when he revives a hero he personally slayed and adopts an orphaned humanoid baby—the last hope to save a dying world. Now bound together, what fate awaits this unlikely trio?', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/7sWrMBhOS1x4RUCr3o2I4ld13fq.jpg', 2, 'tmdb:tv:258348'),
  ('348956379964795057', 'Cleverman', 2016, 'Drama, Crime, Mystery, Sci-Fi & Fantasy, Action & Adventure', 'Leah Purcell, Wayne Blair', null, 'Hunter Page-Lochard, Iain Glen, Rob Collins, Frances O''Connor, Deborah Mailman', 'TV-14', 'In the near future, creatures from ancient Aboriginal mythology endowed with extraordinary physical traits have emerged and must coexist with humans. Known as ''Hairypeople'' they battle for survival in a world that wants to exploit and destroy them. One young man – The Cleverman – struggles with his own power and the responsibility to unite this divided world, but he must first overcome a deep estrangement from his older brother.', 'In the near future, creatures from ancient Aboriginal mythology endowed with extraordinary physical traits have emerged and must coexist with humans. Known as ''Hairypeople'' they battle for survival in a world that wants to exploit and destroy them. One young man – The Cleverman – struggles with his own power and the responsibility to unite this divided world, but he must first overcome a deep estrangement from his older brother.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/ndwQn6o3qTpkN8pHmOeVoToDS6J.jpg', 2, 'tmdb:tv:66633'),
