  ('1060654961222935499', 'Ox Tales', 1987, 'Animation, Comedy', 'Wil Raymakers, Thijs Wilms', null, 'Guido Jonckers, Gerry Middelburg', null, 'The adventures of Ollie the Ox as he runs The Funny Farm, containing possibly every creature known, with his best friend Jack the Turtle, while narrated by a sarcastic Toucan.', 'The adventures of Ollie the Ox as he runs The Funny Farm, containing possibly every creature known, with his best friend Jack the Turtle, while narrated by a sarcastic Toucan.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/agghWvxlyy8LaUxwAG605gwUNH3.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:11749'),
  ('748882648625519945', 'Oxen', 2023, 'Crime, War & Politics', 'Mai Brostrøm, Peter Thorsboe', 'Mai Brostrøm, Jens Henrik Jensen, Peter Thorsboe', 'Jacob Lohmann, Ellen Hillingsø, Josephine Park, Birgitte Hjort Sørensen', null, 'War veteran and former hunter soldier Niels Oxen, Denmark''s most decorated soldier ever. Sent home with war trauma, he tries to create meaning in life and to make everyday life fit together.', 'War veteran and former hunter soldier Niels Oxen, Denmark''s most decorated soldier ever. Sent home with war trauma, he tries to create meaning in life and to make everyday life fit together.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/A1rujCJTNJRfHO02NVWCW1pVCIx.jpg', 2, 'tmdb:tv:237247'),
  ('967695252727408733', 'Oxygen: The Series', 2020, 'Drama', 'Chesshire', null, 'Supanut Lourhaphanich, Chanapoom Thenwong, Thanabat Ngamkamolchai, Phubeth Tharathonchanakul, Kunchanuj Kengkarnka, Rapeepat Aimphan, Thitiwat Limpimproh, Nathalie Ducheine', null, 'Gui, a diligent engineering student, meets Solo, a grieving music major, at a café. Their lives intertwine, blossoming into romance.', 'Gui, a diligent engineering student, meets Solo, a grieving music major, at a café. Their lives intertwine, blossoming into romance.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rA6JPjPcOhWlksf1G6SIIt3gjKE.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:106818'),
  ('125800543299020024', 'Oye Bonita', 2008, 'Drama', null, null, 'Sergio Borrero', 'NR', 'The story revolves mainly around the love between two people who at first are totally different were exiled from their lands in the past due to the ambition of powerful families in the region, the Isazas and a close associate, Antoine Lacouture (the father Diana). Years later, Diana, Antoine''s daughter, meets the Monchi and they fall in love, at this moment the history of the two families (Los Maestre and Los Isazas) intersect again, as Antoine, regretting having taken the lands of the Maestre , decides that it is necessary to return them.', 'The story revolves mainly around the love between two people who at first are totally different were exiled from their lands in the past due to the ambition of powerful families in the region, the Isazas and a close associate, Antoine Lacouture (the father Diana). Years later, Diana, Antoine''s daughter, meets the Monchi and they fall in love, at this moment the history of the two families (Los Maestre and Los Isazas) intersect again, as Antoine, regretting having taken the lands of the Maestre , decides that it is necessary to return them.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3kKapIfcD5XsPhxs595YQn6FYip.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:107135'),
  ('468930295138580086', 'Oz', 1997, 'Crime, Drama', 'Tom Fontana', null, 'Lee Tergesen, Harold Perrineau, Dean Winters, Eamonn Walker, Ernie Hudson, Terry Kinney, Rita Moreno, J.K. Simmons', 'TV-MA', 'The daily lives of prisoners in Emerald City, an experimental unit of the Oswald Maximum Security Prison where ingroups - Muslims, Latinos, Italians, Aryans - stick close to their mutual friends and terrorize their mutual enemies.', 'The daily lives of prisoners in Emerald City, an experimental unit of the Oswald Maximum Security Prison where ingroups - Muslims, Latinos, Italians, Aryans - stick close to their mutual friends and terrorize their mutual enemies.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/oTQ9PUnCgf9CimYeWuDGp8iaT07.jpg', 6, 'tmdb:tv:3322'),
  ('1038691728723497683', 'Ozark', 2017, 'Crime, Drama', 'Bill Dubuque, Mark Williams', null, 'Jason Bateman, Laura Linney, Sofia Hublitz, Skylar Gaertner, Julia Garner, Charlie Tahan, Jessica Frances Dukes, Felix Solis', 'TV-MA', 'A financial adviser drags his family from Chicago to the Missouri Ozarks, where he must launder $500 million in five years to appease a drug boss.', 'A financial adviser drags his family from Chicago to the Missouri Ozarks, where he must launder $500 million in five years to appease a drug boss.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/pCGyPVrI9Fzw6rE1Pvi4BIXF6ET.jpg', 4, 'tmdb:tv:69740'),
  ('259183404149173795', 'Ozzy & Drix', 2002, 'Family, Animation, Comedy', null, null, 'Phil LaMarr, Jeff Bennett, Alanna Ubach, Justin Cowden, Tasia Valenza, Jim Cummings', null, 'Ozzy & Drix, also known as The Fantastic Voyage Adventures of Osmosis Jones & Drixenol and Osmosis Jones: The Animated Series, is an American animated television series based on the Warner Bros. film Osmosis Jones and it was produced by Warner Bros. Animation. It takes place inside the body of teenager Hector Cruz. The series premiered on September 14, 2002 on the Kids'' WB; the final episode aired July 5, 2004. Unlike the original movie it spun off from, Ozzy & Drix was entirely animated and contained no live action. It stars Phil LaMarr as the replacement for Chris Rock as Osmosis Jones, and Jeff Bennett as the replacement for David Hyde Pierce as Drix. As of July 2011, episodes of the series are still available via the Kids WB website. The show also aired on Teletoon in Canada. The show is also slightly less violent than the movie, having the characters treated like people rather than simply cells, and having none of them killed off, unlike the movie where Thrax managed to kill off several cells. There are also new characters that replace the ones from the original movie such as Maria Amino replacing Leah Estrogen, Mayor Spryman replacing Mayor Phlegmming, Sylvian Fischer replacing Tom Colonic, Chief Gluteus replacing The Chief of Police, The Mole replacing Chill the Flu Shot and Scarlet Fever replacing Thrax.', 'Ozzy & Drix, also known as The Fantastic Voyage Adventures of Osmosis Jones & Drixenol and Osmosis Jones: The Animated Series, is an American animated television series based on the Warner Bros. film Osmosis Jones and it was produced by Warner Bros. Animation. It takes place inside the body of teenager Hector Cruz. The series premiered on September 14, 2002 on the Kids'' WB; the final episode aired July 5, 2004. Unlike the original movie it spun off from, Ozzy & Drix was entirely animated and contained no live action. It stars Phil LaMarr as the replacement for Chris Rock as Osmosis Jones, and Jeff Bennett as the replacement for David Hyde Pierce as Drix. As of July 2011, episodes of the series are still available via the Kids WB website. The show also aired on Teletoon in Canada. The show is also slightly less violent than the movie, having the characters treated like people rather than simply cells, and having none of them killed off, unlike the movie where Thrax managed to kill off several cells. There are also new characters that replace the ones from the original movie such as Maria Amino replacing Leah Estrogen, Mayor Spryman replacing Mayor Phlegmming, Sylvian Fischer replacing Tom Colonic, Chief Gluteus replacing The Chief of Police, The Mole replacing Chill the Flu Shot and Scarlet Fever replacing Thrax.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/55Fo6toGvICYq8NTrluBkMPmYWc.jpg', 2, 'tmdb:tv:4684'),
  ('489754834190208983', 'Ozzy and Jack''s World Detour', 2016, 'Reality', null, null, 'Ozzy Osbourne, Jack Osbourne', 'TV-14', 'The self-proclaimed history nerds hit the road in a father-son journey they''ve waited years to take. No roadies, no tour buses and no boundaries - just a bucket list of iconic and historically significant spots that includes Mt. Rushmore, Stonehenge, The Alamo, Roswell, The Jamestown Settlement and Sun Studios and a hit list of some fascinating sights and people that they''ve read about. From a Cold War era Missile Silo to Bletchley Park; from gold miner Rattlesnake Randy''s stream of dreams to vintage tank collector Allan Cors'' private museum of working war machines, Ozzy and Jack get their eyes and hands on history.', 'The self-proclaimed history nerds hit the road in a father-son journey they''ve waited years to take. No roadies, no tour buses and no boundaries - just a bucket list of iconic and historically significant spots that includes Mt. Rushmore, Stonehenge, The Alamo, Roswell, The Jamestown Settlement and Sun Studios and a hit list of some fascinating sights and people that they''ve read about. From a Cold War era Missile Silo to Bletchley Park; from gold miner Rattlesnake Randy''s stream of dreams to vintage tank collector Allan Cors'' private museum of working war machines, Ozzy and Jack get their eyes and hands on history.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3ti0yKOajMdQ3a2IXGZHZpU6Bls.jpg', 3, 'tmdb:tv:67433'),
  ('367704410919784900', 'P-Valley', 2020, 'Drama, Crime', 'Katori Hall', 'Katori Hall', 'Brandee Evans, Nicco Annan, Elarica Johnson, Shannon Thornton, J. Alphonse Nicholson, Parker Sawyers, Harriett D. Foy', 'TV-MA', 'Down deep in the Mississippi Delta, Trap music meets film noir in this kaleidoscopic story of a little-strip-club-that-could and the big characters who come through its doors—the hopeful, the lost, the broken, the ballers, the beautiful, and the damned.', 'Down deep in the Mississippi Delta, Trap music meets film noir in this kaleidoscopic story of a little-strip-club-that-could and the big characters who come through its doors—the hopeful, the lost, the broken, the ballers, the beautiful, and the damned.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/qAuKjGNbcwdhbpxSciak8BFjQ5F.jpg', 3, 'tmdb:tv:87017'),
